-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1107, after review: a deadline that reads the clock, or
-- the world outside the file, is not worked out, written in the WITHIN or
-- reached through a rule. Worked out in the module, `clock duty` comes out 8
-- under one fixed clock and 5 under another, so the answer is the day the
-- command ran on, not the contract's; `env duty` comes out of the
-- environment the command ran in.

IMPORT prelude

TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Alice
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF pay

`clocky` MEANS ((DATE_SERIAL TODAY) MODULO 7) PLUS 3

`env period` MEANS fromMaybe 10 (TONUMBER (fromMaybe "3" (ENV "PERIOD_DAYS")))

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`clock duty` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `clocky` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`today duty` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN ((DATE_SERIAL TODAY) MODULO 7) PLUS 3 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`env duty` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `env period` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
